== a variable that does not exist
  before setenv                getenv:ok  environ-walk:ok  agree:yes
== after setenv, both spellings must see it
  setenv rc=0
  after setenv                 getenv:ok  environ-walk:ok  agree:yes
== overwrite, and overwrite=0 must NOT overwrite
  after overwrite=1            getenv:ok  environ-walk:ok  agree:yes
  after overwrite=0            getenv:ok  environ-walk:ok  agree:yes
== enough new variables to force a reallocation
  original still visible       getenv:ok  environ-walk:ok  agree:yes
  the last filler              getenv:ok  environ-walk:ok  agree:yes
  environ has at least the 65 we added: yes
== unsetenv, and both spellings must stop seeing it
  unsetenv rc=0
  after unsetenv               getenv:ok  environ-walk:ok  agree:yes
== putenv, which stores the caller's buffer rather than copying
  putenv rc=0
  after putenv                 getenv:ok  environ-walk:ok  agree:yes
done
